```java
// One Boot app auto-wires Spring MVC, Spring Data, and Spring Security
@SpringBootApplication
public class OrderApplication {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        SpringApplication.run(OrderApplication.class, args);
    }
}

@RestController                              // Spring MVC
@RequestMapping("/api/orders")
class OrderController {
    private final OrderRepository repo;
    OrderController(OrderRepository repo) { this.repo = repo; }

    @GetMapping
    @PreAuthorize("hasRole('USER')")        // Spring Security
    List<Order> all() { return repo.findAll(); }   // Spring Data
}

@Entity
class Order { @Id @GeneratedValue Long id; String item; }

interface OrderRepository extends JpaRepository<Order, Long> {} // Spring Data JPA
```

```java
@Configuration
class JsonConfig {
    @Bean
    Jackson2ObjectMapperBuilderCustomizer apiDates() {
        return builder -> builder.simpleDateFormat("yyyy-MM-dd");
    }
}
```

Use a documented customization hook when only one behavior must change. Replacing the complete `ObjectMapper` or `DataSource` can make the related missing-bean default back off, which means the application owns more configuration.

